    <p class="note"><strong>How we rate ease:</strong> 5 is door-to-gate with no change and little waiting. 4 is a quick change inside the same system. 3 is a shared bus whose wait we haven't timed yet. These ratings are provisional until we time each trip ourselves. The Skyliner times are the same ones we use for Pop Century, because the two resorts share a station.</p>

    <h3>Skyliner vs. bus: the honest version</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hours:</strong> the Skyliner opens an hour before Early Theme Park Entry at EPCOT or Hollywood Studios and closes 90 minutes after those parks close. Buses and other resort transportation start 45 minutes before park opening and run up to an hour after closing.</li>
      <li><strong>The EPCOT late-night catch:</strong> on nights when EPCOT has Extended Evening Hours, the Skyliner only runs between EPCOT and the Riviera. The route serving Caribbean Beach, Pop Century and Art of Animation isn't available, so plan on a bus.</li>
      <li><strong>Weather:</strong> it keeps running in light rain but stops for lightning or high wind. In summer storm season, keep the bus in mind as a backup.</li>
      <li><strong>Annual closure:</strong> Jan 24–30, 2027, with free buses instead.</li>
      <li><strong>Pop Century is next door.</strong> The Generation Gap Bridge links the two resorts, so you can walk over for Everything POP or hop a Pop Century bus if it arrives first.</li>
    </ul>
