  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The Big Blue Pool</strong> in the Finding Nemo courtyard is the main pool. Disney calls it the largest hotel pool at Walt Disney World and lists it at more than 308,527 gallons. There's a zero-entry side, the Schoolyard Sprayground for little kids, and Squirt's Righteous Reef playground if they want to stay dry. The Drop Off pool bar is next to it. It's also the busiest.</li>
      <li><strong>Cozy Cone Pool</strong> in the Cars courtyard is smaller, at 74,740 gallons, with cone-shaped cabanas around the edge.</li>
      <li><strong>Flippin' Fins Pool</strong> in the Little Mermaid courtyard holds 103,642 gallons and is usually a quieter option if you're staying in that section.</li>
      <li>24-hour self-service laundry rooms sit near all three pools.</li>
      <li>Also on site: Pixel Play Arcade in Animation Hall, campfires, Movies Under the Stars on select nights, a second playground (The Boneyard) in the Lion King courtyard, and a 1.38-mile jogging trail around Hourglass Lake.</li>
    </ul>
